* Public 16-sample coherent sine: bin 1 of 16 (3.125 MHz), 0.72 V amplitude around 1.8 V, typical / 3.30 V / 27 C.
* Grading uses another amplitude and phase. Every ideal sample lies at least 0.14 LSB from a threshold for any
* sampling instant from the start of the clock source's rising edge to 1.5 ns after it.
* Zero-state start: every source ramps up from 0 V over the first 5 ns, and power is metered from t = 0, so
* the circuit pays for any charge it stores (see spec/README.md).
.include "/opt/gf180/pdk/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/xyce/design.xyce"
.lib "/opt/gf180/pdk/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/xyce/sm141064.xyce" typical
.include "/app/circuit.spi"
.options device temp=27
VSS vss 0 0
VSUP vdd vss PWL(0 0 5n 3.3)
VRP vrefp_s vss PWL(0 0 5n 2.6)
RRP vrefp_s vrefp 10
VRN vrefn_s vss PWL(0 0 5n 1.0)
RRN vrefn_s vrefn 10
VCK clk_s vss PULSE(0 3.3 10n 0.3n 0.3n 9.4n 20n)
RCK clk_s clk 50
BSIG vin_b vss V={min(1,TIME/5n)*(1.8+0.72*sin(2*pi*3.125e+06*TIME+351*pi/180))}
VSIG vin_s vin_b 0
RSIG vin_s vin 50
XADC vss vdd vrefn vrefp clk vin b2 b1 b0 flash_adc_3bit
CB2 b2 vss 50f
CB1 b1 vss 50f
CB0 b0 vss 50f

.tran 50p 371n 0 0.2n
* the grader reads Xyce's raw file (every node and source current); this line is for your own plots
.print tran format=csv v(clk) v(vin) v(b2) v(b1) v(b0)
.end
